  "id": "chain/a-first-post-past-the-reentry-budget-binds-nothing",
  "title": "A first post from the room's work past its cascade's reentry budget is stored BLOCKED and binds nothing: no host binding, no attachment, no ON_CHANNEL_ATTACHED; a room the host channel was detached from refuses it first",
  "rules": [
    "§10.5 The host's own voice",
    "§8.3 Reentry cap",
    "§9.5.1 The room's work outside the lock"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-10.5-034",
    "RK-8.3-035",
    "RK-8.3-038"
  ],
  "reentrancy": [
    "inject@cascade",
    "inject@locked",
    "inject@admitted"
  ],
  "notes": "max_chain_depth is 1, so the cascade's budget is 10 passes. In room-1, ws's delivery of the message makes ten injections, which draw them, then a first post, which is past the budget: stored BLOCKED before any attach, with the visibility the host channel's binding at its defaults gives, all. Its host channel is not bound and ON_CHANNEL_ATTACHED does not run; the next post, outside that work, attaches it once. In room-2 the host channel was detached before: the same post is refused channel_not_bound, the revocation checked before its pass, and nothing of it is stored. In room-3, room-4 and room-5 the same ten injections and first post come from a locked hook, an off-lock hook and an ASYNC hook's body: each post is stored BLOCKED and binds nothing, and posted again with its key it is a replay, which returns that record and binds nothing either.",
